// The message queue, bound. `polyp_queue.h` holds the whole thing: three rings
// of ints (plus the edit ring's text) and static inline functions, compiled
// into whichever translation unit includes the header, so `library` has
// nothing to link and names libc only because a section must name something.
//
// `polyp_poll` answers -1 when the queue is empty, which is why its Kelp return
// type is `i32` rather than the `usize` an index would be.
pub extern fun polyp_post(id: i32)

pub extern fun polyp_poll().R: i32

// The edit channel: a program with no user asks the loop to set an entry's
// text, which fires the entry's real `changed` signal. `polyp_poll_edit`
// answers the entry's position in the current tree, or -1 when none is
// pending, and `polyp_poll_edit_text` is the text of the edit just polled.
pub extern fun polyp_post_edit(index: i32, text: str)
pub extern fun polyp_poll_edit().R: i32
pub extern fun polyp_poll_edit_text().R: str

// The focus channel: the same idea for `gtk_widget_grab_focus`, so a smoke run
// can put the focus somewhere and then watch a patch keep it there. It answers
// the entry's position in the current tree, or -1 when none is pending.
pub extern fun polyp_post_focus(index: i32)
pub extern fun polyp_poll_focus().R: i32
